 "source": "HDB, 99.co, DBS",
 "caption": "Applying for the November BTO? The label on your flat could lock you in for 10 years. 🏢\n\nAbout 7,960 flats across six towns, and HDB confirms each project's label at launch.\nStandard: 5 year minimum occupation period, then you can rent out the whole flat.\nPlus and Prime: 10 years before you can sell, and you can never rent out the whole flat. When you sell, HDB takes back a share of the price, set per project. Past launches ranged from about 6% to 9%.\n\nSave this before you pick your flat 👇\n\nHDB rules. Recovery is a % of the resale price or valuation, whichever is higher.",
